<title>FRANCE: Axa-UAP rises over one pct on Sun Life.</title>
<headline>Axa-UAP rises over one pct on Sun Life.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French insurance group AXA rose by more than one percent after news that Sun Life was buying its Equity and Law and AEL Investment Managers for 690 million stg and Axa insurance for 70 million stg.</p>
<p>Axa-UAP will issue 247.56 million new shares at 307p per share to Axa-UAP, already Sun Life's majority owner. At 0904 GMT, AXA was up 0.86 percent at 373.20 francs. It had been as high as 374.90 francs.</p>
</text>
